{"id": "EUVD-2026-70333", "enisaUuid": "ceae3289-2eeb-3f67-be0f-9518293eb40f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/huge_memory: initialise workingset state before folio split\n\nxas_try_split() adds __GFP_ACCOUNT for page-cache xa_nodes, but\n__folio_split() leaves the xa_state's xa_lru unset.  That lets a live,\nmemcg-charged xa_node exist without being linked into the mapping's\nshadow_nodes list_lru; when reclaim later walks the list_lru it trips\nVM_WARN_ON(!css_is_dying()).\n\nUse mapping_set_update() to install both the workingset update callback\nand the shadow_nodes list_lru on the xa_state.", "datePublished": "2026-09-03T08:21:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-11T13:47:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc87b56b43c9143f2405e434cff1530c3488b571", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d858f7c9fc514f1d9d3be7d00b2dd4e2f2383b55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aca1f2d5de17e138bc6c4859126b77e516b82541"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80729", "GHSA-p2p8-6fmx-rfj9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05bf69b2-91ee-3d30-92d7-c97490568c29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "4ed21613-4bf7-323f-8dc9-ede8ff70a812", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "879aacc6-e6bd-395b-ae7a-86f4da8e9f04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "93c8d5bf-c7cc-3a07-bab2-21b71eea2424", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "a323eeb5-995d-3377-bff8-5b7e6884288f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "c2020b58-ac59-3435-9d95-305fc8c00c5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "58729c04cf1092b87aeef0bf0998c9e2e4771133 <d858f7c9fc514f1d9d3be7d